/target

# Cargo.lock is committed deliberately: this workspace produces binaries, and
# the lock is what pins the calamine fork to an exact commit. Without it a
# `branch = ...` dependency would drift silently.

# Confidential or user-supplied workbooks. Never commit real spreadsheets:
# they routinely contain commercial, personal or financial data.
/private/
*.private.xlsx
*.private.xlsb

# fastembed's default model cache, if anything ever falls back to it
.fastembed_cache/

# The demo workbook's flat-ODS source. Regenerable from `eg-fixtures`, which is
# the actual source of truth, and large enough that committing it beside the
# converted files would double the fixture for nothing.
tests/fixtures/demo/*.fods

# A large demo workbook, generated on demand to show what the scale claims rest
# on. Not committed: it is minutes of LibreOffice and tens of megabytes, and
# one command reproduces it.
#   cargo run --release -p eg-fixtures -- --rows 400000 --out demo --formats xlsx
/demo/
